---
title: Part IV - unstructured source update and retraining
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Job as monitor_unstructured
    participant SM as source_monitor_service
    participant Lake as Data lake (raw)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant RT as retraining_service
    participant ML as ml.src pipeline
    participant Reg as Model registry

    Job->>SM: check_source()
    SM->>DB: resolve DS010 via DATASET -> DATA_ASSET
    SM->>Lake: read watched file
    SM->>SM: SHA-256 of the bytes
    SM->>DB: compare with DATA_ASSET.SHA256

    alt checksum unchanged
        SM-->>Job: no change
        Note over Job,DB: No ML_RUN is created.<br/>Running the monitor again<br/>changes nothing.
    else checksum changed
        SM->>Lake: copy bytes to versions/ (never overwrite)
        SM->>DB: mark previous asset Superseded
        SM->>DB: INSERT DATA_ASSET (new version, new checksum)
        Note over SM,DB: File first, catalogue row second.<br/>A crash between the two leaves an<br/>unreferenced file, not a dangling row.

        Job->>RT: retrain(new asset)
        RT->>DB: INSERT ML_RUN (Status = Running)
        Note over RT,DB: Committed on its own, so a<br/>failure that follows is still recorded.

        RT->>ML: extract -> chunk -> clean
        RT->>ML: TF-IDF -> candidate K -> K-means
        RT->>ML: top terms, representative passages

        alt pipeline succeeded
            RT->>Reg: write versioned artifacts
            RT->>DB: INSERT DOCUMENT_CHUNK
            RT->>DB: INSERT ML_CLUSTER_RESULT
            RT->>DB: INSERT ML_CLUSTER_SUMMARY (HumanReviewed = FALSE)
            RT->>DB: UPDATE ML_RUN = Completed + metrics
            Note over RT,DB: One transaction. Completing the run<br/>is what activates the model, so a<br/>partially loaded model cannot serve.
            RT-->>Job: new model active, all clusters unreviewed
        else pipeline failed
            RT->>DB: UPDATE ML_RUN = Failed + error
            Note over RT,DB: No chunk, assignment, or summary row<br/>was written. The previous completed<br/>run is still the latest completed run,<br/>so it keeps serving with no repair.
            RT-->>Job: previous model preserved
        end
    end
